course: dictionary
lesson: 1928
title: Comfy and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Comfy is an informal word, the kind people use in friendly, relaxed talk. It means comfortable: soft, cosy and pleasant to sit, lie or be in. «Ollie liked to play lying on his tummy on the floor; it was comfy for twenty minutes.» The floor was soft and pleasant for Ollie, so comfy means comfortable here.
explain: Comfy can also describe a feeling. When you feel relaxed and at ease, you feel comfy inside. «Then Taffy owns up, not feeling very comfy, that she gave him the picture.» Taffy is not relaxed at all, so this comfy is about her feelings, not about a sofa.
explain: To choose the right meaning, look at the words around comfy. A sofa, a bed or a chair means the first meaning. A person who is worried or guilty means the second. Then swap in comfortable: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Comfy is an adjective, and it is informal, so it fits friendly, chatty talk better than formal writing.
fact: Its other forms are comfier and comfiest, as in «the comfiest chair in the house».
fact: Comfy means comfortable: soft, cosy and pleasant to sit, lie or be in.
fact: Comfy can also mean relaxed and at ease, as in «not feeling very comfy».
fact: In Chinese, «shūfu» means comfortable, so «hǎo shūfu» on a soft sofa means «so comfy».
exercise: «Ollie liked to play lying on his tummy on the floor; it was comfy for twenty minutes.» What does comfy mean here? | *Soft and pleasant to lie on | Very loud | Wet and muddy | Cold and hard
exercise: «Then Taffy owns up, not feeling very comfy, that she gave him the picture.» What does comfy mean in this sentence? | Hungry | *Not relaxed or at ease | Very relaxed and happy | Soft and cosy
exercise: Which word is the form of comfy that means the most comfy of all? | comfier | comfy | comfortable | *comfiest
test: Jo says, «Your bed is comfy.» Which word could replace comfy here? | Sharp | Noisy | *Comfortable | Cold
test: Which sentence uses comfy to mean relaxed and at ease? | *I feel comfy with my new class. | The bed is comfy tonight. | The chair is comfy by the fire. | The sofa is comfy and soft.
exam: What does informal mean for the word comfy? | Used only by very old people | Used only in science reports | Hard to say or spell | *Used in relaxed, friendly talk rather than formal writing
